.TH GPSTREAM 8 "2026-09-14" "gpstream 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpstream \- high-throughput logical copy of data between Greenplum 6 clusters

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpstream
.I command
.RI "[ " flags "] "

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gpstream
copies logical data between two Greenplum 6 clusters over a direct high-speed
network (source -> destination)
.B "without any intermediate storage"
, with snapshot consistency, crash-recovery, background index rebuild,
redistribution accounting, and a fully deterministic
.BR \-\-dry-run
plan.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Execute the copy: stream source to dest with no intermediate storage (v4 §8).
.TP
.B dry-run
Plan the copy without executing (\-\-timeout S bounds the plan; \-\-plan-file F emits it).
.TP
.B status
Report operation state (\-\-operation-id <id>).
.TP
.B resume
Resume an interrupted operation (\-\-operation-id <id>).
.TP
.BR cleanup
.IR <operation-id>
Remove operation state (\-\-all-incomplete). With \-\-mode drop \-\-dest <connstring>, also drop the destination objects this operation created (surviving staging, renamed-in or created final tables, renamed-in schemas) to restore the pre-operation state (F-02). Destructive: requires \-\-yes.
.TP
.B doctor
Self-diagnose source/dest clusters; output PASS/FAIL/WARN (this build).
.TP
.B selftest
Internal sanity checks: schema, checksums, limiter, plan determinism, framing (this build).
.TP
.BR man
.IR "[ topic ] "
Print the built-in man page (M4).

.SH OPTIONS (run / dry-run, §8)
.TP
.BR \-source
.RI "[ " connstr " ] "
source cluster connection string.
.TP
.BR \-dest
.RI "[ " connstr " ] "
destination cluster connection string.
.TP
.BR \-full | \-db D | \-schema D.S | \-table D.S.T
Selection; combinable.
.TP
.BR \-metadata\-only | \-data\-only
Copy only metadata, or only data (default: both).
.TP
.BR \-skip\-conflicts " (alias " \-skip\-existing ")
Skip conflicting tables and continue.
.BR \-overwrite | \-truncate | \-append
Replace / truncate-then-load / append the destination object.
Default (none of the above): a conflict
.B "stops the run"
(nothing overwritten, nothing skipped).
.TP
.BR \-rename\-db
.IR "src=dst"
Create the destination database under another name.
.TP
.BR \-rename\-schema
.IR "src=dst"
Create the destination schema under another name.
.TP
.BR \-compress
.I "none|zlib|zstd[:1-19]"
Stream compression; recommended
.BR zstd .
.TP
.BR \-rate\-limit
.I "Gbps"
Total and per-pair rate limit.
.TP
.BR \-workers\-per\-pair
.I N
Workers per host-pair.
.TP
.BR \-data\-port\-range
.I "a-b"
Range of data ports.
.TP
.BR \-auto\-resume
.I N
Auto-resume after failure (N >= 0; default 0 = manual).
.TP
.BR \-verify
.I "full|sample|off"
Verification depth; default sample.
.TP
.BR \-index\-workers
.I N
Index builder workers (default: half host CPU);
.BR \-no\-indexes
defer indexes.
.TP
.BR \-no\-redistribute | \-skew\-threshold X
Skip redistribution, or set the skew threshold.
.TP
.BR \-ssl\-cert \-ssl\-key \-ssl\-ca \-ssl\-min\-tls
TLS configuration (mTLS + chain validation).
.TP
.BR \-dry\-run | \-timeout S | \-plan\-file F
Planning options.
.TP
.BR \-config F | \-log\-level L | \-quiet | \-debug
Configuration and logging.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
Configuration precedence: CLI > environment > config file (TOML) > defaults. Secrets are
taken
.B "only"
from 0600 files or
.B GPSTREAM_*
environment variables,
.B "never from argv"
(FR-08). Recognised variables include
.BR GPSTREAM_RATE_LIMIT ,
.BR GPSTREAM_WORKERS_PER_PAIR ,
.BR GPSTREAM_COMPRESS ,
.BR GPSTREAM_LOG_LEVEL ,
.BR GPSTREAM_AUTO_RESUME ,
.BR GPSTREAM_SSL_CERT ,
.BR GPSTREAM_SSL_KEY ,
.BR GPSTREAM_SSL_CA .

.SH SEE ALSO
.RI [ .TH gpstream]
man
.BR "gpstream(8)" ,
.RI [ .TP ]
docs/architecture, docs/adr/000, docs/adr/001.

.SH NOTES
M0 provides
.BR doctor
and
.BR selftest
as working commands; run/status/resume/cleanup execute real transfers.
